From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: wcn36xx: bound SMD transmit FIFO waits

Qualcomm SMD rpmsg_send() can wait indefinitely for TX FIFO space,
so the existing firmware response timeout cannot bound the operation.
Retry rpmsg_trysend() only on -EAGAIN, with a HAL_MSG_TIMEOUT deadline,
and preserve other transport errors and the separate response timeout.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>

---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/smd.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/smd.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/smd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/smd.c
@@ -431,7 +431,16 @@
 
 	init_completion(&wcn->hal_rsp_compl);
 	start = jiffies;
-	ret = rpmsg_send(wcn->smd_channel, wcn->hal_buf, len);
+	do {
+		ret = rpmsg_trysend(wcn->smd_channel, wcn->hal_buf, len);
+		if (ret != -EAGAIN)
+			break;
+		if (time_after_eq(jiffies, start + msecs_to_jiffies(HAL_MSG_TIMEOUT))) {
+			ret = -ETIMEDOUT;
+			break;
+		}
+		usleep_range(1000, 2000);
+	} while (1);
 	if (ret) {
 		wcn36xx_err("HAL TX failed for req %d\n", req_type);
 		goto out;
